# do not delete me
#
# Git tracks files, not directories, so this directory would vanish from
# the next clone without a file in it. This is that file. It ignores
# nothing on purpose — see `keepMarker` in schemas/cat-harness.ts.
#
# interaction/
# How a PERSON wants to be asked — committed, read at session start by every
# agent. `context` by the same test as agent memory: read during a process,
# never written by one, changed when a person states a preference. It sat in
# `.harness/`, undeclared, until 2026-09-20, which this repository's own
# dot-prefix guard forbids: a dot-prefixed directory is absent from a plain
# `ls`, from most file browsers and from a forge's web tree, and the file
# read at the start of every session was in the one place the conventions
# reject. The path is also `harness.config.json`'s `interaction` key, which
# defaults here — the declaration and the config now name the same place
# instead of one of them being a literal nobody checks.
